+{"id":"fabro-e4fa","title":"Tighten planner sd call economy","status":"open","type":"task","priority":2,"createdAt":"2026-09-02T19:59:23.883Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-03T17:28:50.784Z","description":"In .fabro/workflows/develop/prompts/planner.md, make the rule conditional and checkable (sd list only if sd ready output is truncated or lacks needed blocker info) and add sd ready --format json to the command table. In run 01M0TXPX09279433MGWSWPVVP4 planner@1 ran sd ready then sd list with byte-identical ~3.3 KB payloads, and used a --format flag on ready not listed in the table. Expected effect: one fewer tracker call and ~10 s less deliberation per cycle while keeping the no-invented-flags rule credible.","labels":["revision"]}
+{"id":"fabro-e702","title":"Require timeout_ms on compile/test shells and ban placeholder appends in implementer prompt","status":"open","type":"task","priority":1,"createdAt":"2026-09-02T20:15:59.086Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-03T17:28:50.888Z","description":"In .fabro/workflows/develop/prompts/implementer.md ('Your job this pass') add two hard rules: (a) any shell call that compiles or tests MUST pass timeout_ms of at least 60000 — run 01M0WWKAQCWZC0Q0JK019H0ZC7's chained append+gofmt+vet+test died at the default 10s with zero output (seq 163-164, 10,345ms, is_error), forcing a blind re-run; (b) never append placeholder code to fix later — the implementer appended a mangled placeholder test via heredoc, then head -n -28 cut the wrong lines leaving a dangling comment, costing ~48s and ~6 wasted calls (a third of its 149.5s stage). Expected effect: implementer pass ~100s instead of ~150s and the silent-timeout failure class eliminated.","labels":["revision"]}
+{"id":"fabro-6a5a","title":"Fix PR postlude: disable auto-merge and stop the failing PR-body model call","status":"open","type":"task","priority":1,"createdAt":"2026-09-02T20:15:59.090Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-03T17:28:45.644Z","description":"In the run-spec pull_request block (see .fabro/project.toml [run.pull_request]) set auto_merge=false — the auto-merge GraphQL call deterministically fails ('Auto merge is not allowed for this repository') despite auto_merge=true — and fix or disable the PR-body LLM call, which failed ('No object generated: Failed to parse response as JSON', worker log 16:44:33 in run 01M0WWKAQCWZC0Q0JK019H0ZC7) and fell back to a skeleton. The postlude burned ~53s after the exit node finished (16:43:46 to 16:44:39), 18% of the 293s wall, and emits two warn-level failures every run. Expected effect: run completes ~50s sooner with two fewer recurring warnings. Partial overlap with open fabro-9f97 (journal-only-diff case); this covers real-diff runs.","labels":["revision"]}
+{"id":"fabro-a23f","title":"Make implementer journal report errored or timed-out tool calls","status":"open","type":"task","priority":2,"createdAt":"2026-09-02T20:16:05.689Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-03T17:28:46.762Z","description":"In .fabro/workflows/develop/prompts/implementer.md (Journal section) add: a tool call that errored or timed out ALWAYS goes in observations, even when recovered — name the call, the timeout, and the workaround. Run 01M0WWKAQCWZC0Q0JK019H0ZC7's implementer journaled observations as none (seq 187) despite a 10.3s shell timeout, an is_error grep, and a signature change forcing edits at ~28 test call-sites; the signal reached the improve loop only via event-stream archaeology. Complements open fabro-b809 (mandatory painpoints array). Expected effect: friction self-reports on the run where it happens, so prompt fixes surface through the journal pipeline instead of manual analysis.","labels":["revision"]}
+{"id":"fabro-8d2c","title":"Raise preamble_budget_kb from 24 to 32 — evidence blob detour persists","status":"open","type":"task","priority":2,"createdAt":"2026-09-02T20:16:05.701Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-03T17:28:46.495Z","description":"In .fabro/workflows/develop/workflow.fabro (graph attr, currently 24 after the 12-to-24 raise) set preamble_budget_kb=32. Run 01M0WWKAQCWZC0Q0JK019H0ZC7's 22.1KB evidence capture (seq 209) still rendered as a blob ref in the reviewer prompt (seq 218) because 22.9KB + tester section + context keys (~28KB aggregate) exceeds 24KB; the reviewer recovered via one 102ms read_file, but the same detour produced the false rejection in run 01M0SS23MJM8972CBJD0SP7T4Q. Expected effect: evidence arrives inline in the preamble, one fewer tool round-trip per review, preview-misread mode removed. SUPERSEDES the targets of open seeds fabro-83f9 and fabro-35ab (both still say raise from 12) — close or amend those to avoid triple filing.","labels":["revision"]}
+{"id":"fabro-f4cd","title":"Fast-path planner to sd show when the goal names a seed id","status":"open","type":"task","priority":2,"createdAt":"2026-09-02T20:16:14.678Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-03T17:28:51.164Z","description":"In .fabro/workflows/develop/prompts/planner.md step 1 add: if the goal names a seed id, run sd show <id> directly; run sd ready only when it doesn't, and never run sd list to re-confirm a count sd ready already printed. Run 01M0WWKAQCWZC0Q0JK019H0ZC7's goal named fabro-f74b; sd ready returned exactly that one seed (seq 39), yet the planner still ran sd list --format json purely to double-check the count (reasoning at seq 67), after sd show + sd update + two globs + a full 10.4KB read of main.go — 7 tool calls and 76.6s inference for a single-candidate claim. Expected effect: two fewer shell calls and one LLM turn on named-seed runs, the common case for this workflow's goals. Overlaps the tracker-empty case in open fabro-b382 and fabro-e4fa; this covers the named-seed case.","labels":["revision"]}
+{"id":"fabro-f8f8","title":"Derive files_touched from the stage git diff, not write-tool calls","status":"open","type":"task","priority":2,"createdAt":"2026-09-02T20:16:14.687Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-03T17:28:51.244Z","description":"Engine-side: compute stage files_touched from the stage checkpoint's git diff (the data already exists per checkpoint, seq 194 of run 01M0WWKAQCWZC0Q0JK019H0ZC7). That run's implementer metadata reported files_touched: [README.md, main.go] (seq 190) while the actual stage diff — and the evidence capture — shows fib_test.go at +159/-28, the largest product change of the run, missed because the file was edited through shell (perl, head, heredoc append) invisible to write-tool instrumentation. Expected effect: accurate per-stage change attribution with no silently missing files for any consumer keying on files_touched.","labels":["revision"]}
+{"id":"fabro-50de","title":"Classify evidence-pipe workarounds as painpoints in develop stage prompts","status":"open","type":"task","priority":2,"createdAt":"2026-09-03T17:36:45.921Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-03T17:36:45.921Z","description":"In .fabro/workflows/develop/prompts/reviewer.md and implementer.md (Journal section), add one sentence: a successful workaround of the evidence pipe, tools, or scripts is a painpoint with its fix idea, not an observation. In run 01M11P68SHFS165HP9ATK6094V every stage emitted painpoints: [] while the blob-truncation fallback, the per-seed-base idea, and the missing python3/node were logged under observations, where the improve loop that keys on painpoints may never act on them. Orthogonal to open seed fabro-b809 (channel emission, not content classification). Expected effect: genuine fixes reach the improve loop journal on the run where they happen.","labels":["revision"]}
+{"id":"fabro-a0fe","title":"Tell develop reviewer to read blob refs with read_file offset/limit","status":"open","type":"task","priority":2,"createdAt":"2026-09-03T17:36:46.015Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-03T17:36:46.015Z","description":"In .fabro/workflows/develop/prompts/reviewer.md (Input section, blob-ref paragraph), state that blob files are read with read_file (offset/limit for large blobs). reviewer@3 in run 01M11P68SHFS165HP9ATK6094V found python3/node unavailable and improvised nu str substring chunking on a 58.1 KB evidence blob because the prompt never mentions the sanctioned path. Expected effect: removes improvised-read friction; pairs with open seeds fabro-8d2c/fabro-d97b.","labels":["revision"]}
+{"id":"fabro-ee2c","title":"Require ml record for implementer near-miss tool lessons","status":"open","type":"task","priority":2,"createdAt":"2026-09-03T17:36:46.111Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-03T17:36:46.111Z","description":"In .fabro/workflows/develop/prompts/implementer.md step 6 (or the stage-journal hook), make ml record mandatory for near-miss tool lessons. implementer@1's edit_file old_string swallowed a whole test loop body in fib_test.go, was caught only by re-reading, and the lesson went into the run journal that no future session loads; implementer@2 then spent 284 s / 0.49 USD (42% of run agent cost) editing the same 1,100-line table-literal file without the guardrail. Expected effect: the next implementer inherits the scoped-old_string guardrail via ml prime --files.","labels":["revision"]}
+{"id":"fabro-169b","title":"Declare lesson_capture in the implementer node's context_allow_keys","status":"open","type":"task","priority":1,"createdAt":"2026-09-03T17:46:38.461Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-03T17:46:38.461Z","description":"Seed fabro-f831 makes lesson_capture a required key of the Implemented JSON in .fabro/workflows/develop/prompts/implementer.md, but workflow.fabro's implementer node still declares context_allow_keys=implementation_summary,journal, so the undeclared key drops as drift on every future pass (per fabro-900e comment). Change: one line in workflow.fabro implementer node — context_allow_keys=implementation_summary,lesson_capture,journal; optionally also add it to the reviewer's preamble_allow_keys. Effect: the enforced record-or-skip answer lands durably instead of being discarded.","labels":["revision"]}
+{"id":"fabro-3d2d","title":"Add a repo-layout map to the planner prompt or AGENTS.md","status":"open","type":"task","priority":1,"createdAt":"2026-09-03T17:46:38.588Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-03T17:46:38.588Z","description":"planner@1 burned 354.7 s / $0.219 of the $0.547 total (50,460 input tokens) on ~10 exploratory calls just to locate dev-loop assets that live at .fabro/workflows/develop/ in the same repo; planner@2 with the layout in context took 98 s / $0.064. Change: add a 5-line Repo layout section to AGENTS.md (loaded as memory into every stage) or .fabro/workflows/develop/prompts/planner.md: gofib at repo root; dev-loop assets at .fabro/workflows/develop/; reviews at .fabro/reviews/; journals at .fabro/journal/. Effect: first planner pass drops from ~6 min toward ~100 s — roughly −4.5 min wall and −$0.15 per run. Distinct from the sd call-economy seeds (fabro-e4fa/f4cd/1399): those tune tracker calls, this removes filesystem orientation calls.","labels":["revision"]}
+{"id":"fabro-4b57","title":"Emit a loop-work diff in evidence.nu when only churn files changed","status":"open","type":"task","priority":1,"createdAt":"2026-09-03T17:46:44.453Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-03T17:46:44.453Z","description":"Seeds targeting .fabro/ paths are classified as loop churn by .fabro/workflows/develop/scripts/evidence.nu, so captures read seed-work=0 files +0/-0 and reviewers must run their own git diff. Change: in evidence.nu, when seed_rows is empty but churn_rows is not, emit the per-seed (claim-base) diff of changed loop files under a loop-work diff section — the per-seed diff-base machinery from fabro-1e9f's theme already provides the base. Effect: reviews of dev-loop seeds verify from context, removing the per-review git detour. Cross-ref: fabro-1e9f (diff against last seed boundary) is the same machinery at run level.","labels":["revision"]}
+{"id":"fabro-a5de","title":"Ban sd prime in develop planner and implementer prompts","status":"open","type":"task","priority":2,"createdAt":"2026-09-03T17:46:44.627Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-03T17:46:44.627Z","description":"planner@1 executed sd prime because AGENTS.md memory instructs it, pulling a 4.7 KB banner whose Session Close Protocol mandates sd close + sd sync && git push — both reserved for the deterministic Closeout; the planner journaled that an LLM skimming the banner could comply. Change: one line in .fabro/workflows/develop/prompts/planner.md and prompts/implementer.md: never run sd prime in this loop — its close/push protocol contradicts the role rules and the context brief supersedes it. Effect: removes a directly contradicting instruction from every stage context and eliminates the mis-close/push risk. Complements the AGENTS.md boilerplate fix in fabro-cc23.","labels":["revision"]}
+{"id":"fabro-3d04","title":"Make the authorized-exception pattern standing in the implementer prompt","status":"open","type":"task","priority":2,"createdAt":"2026-09-03T17:46:49.669Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-03T17:46:49.669Z","description":"Briefs carry manual override prose (fabro-f831's brief opened with CONTRADICTION RESOLVED authorizing exactly one .fabro/ file), and implementer@2 journaled that the pattern recurred across fabro-7e44 and fabro-f831 and deserves a platform-level convention. Change: in .fabro/workflows/develop/prompts/implementer.md's Platform scope section add: exception — a brief that names a specific platform file authorizes editing exactly that file. Effect: planner briefs shed roughly a third of their text and the implementer no longer reconciles a contradiction before starting.","labels":["revision"]}
+{"id":"fabro-50f8","title":"Require null-path exercises when editing workflow scripts","status":"open","type":"task","priority":2,"createdAt":"2026-09-03T17:46:49.774Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-03T17:46:49.774Z","description":"implementer@1 found a latent crash — a string-typed Nushell param rejects runtime null, which would have crashed evidence.nu's no-seed-in-progress path (mulch mx-0b966a) — surfaced only because that brief happened to demand fallback/null/empty-diff exercises; the gate's nu-check is syntax-only. Change: add to .fabro/workflows/develop/prompts/implementer.md step 2: when editing workflow scripts, exercise the null/no-seed/fallback paths via nu -c before finishing. Effect: rarely-hit paths get verified on every workflow-script seed, not only when a brief remembers to ask.","labels":["revision"]}
+{"id":"fabro-01b9","title":"Path-scope the tester gate for prompt-only seeds","status":"open","type":"task","priority":2,"createdAt":"2026-09-03T17:46:57.823Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-03T17:46:57.823Z","description":"Both tester runs executed the full Go gate (build/vet/test, 11.1 s cold, 1.1 s cached) on a tree where gofib was never touched — both seeds changed only .fabro/ and .mulch/ files. Change: route a lite path (e.g. a just qualitygate-lite running nu-check + sync) from the same tester node when only .fabro//.md files changed. Effect: seconds per cycle, and a structurally meaningless check disappears from dev-loop seeds; lowest impact of this run's findings.","labels":["revision"]}
+{"id":"fabro-7fba","title":"Add evidence to the reviewer's preamble_stages_ignore","status":"open","type":"task","priority":2,"createdAt":"2026-09-03T17:46:57.954Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-03T17:46:57.954Z","description":"reviewer@2's prompt carried the identical ~2 KB evidence capture twice plus two tester sections and the prior cycle's closeout block, because preamble_stages_ignore keeps tester+evidence per visit and command.output dedups into the evidence stage section rather than replacing it. Change: in workflow.fabro, add evidence to the reviewer node's preamble_stages_ignore — the current capture still arrives via the command.output context key, which the prompt already teaches the reviewer to read as a blob ref. Effect: ~2 KB less preamble per review cycle and stale prior-cycle captures disappear. Complements open fabro-699f (latest-visit rendering) with a different mechanism.","labels":["revision"]}
 {"id":"fabro-meta-c454","title":"develop planner: close the ## Context input contract (preamble_allow_keys) — implementer already closed","status":"open","type":"task","priority":2,"createdAt":"2026-09-03T21:05:17.459Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-03T21:05:17.459Z","description":"Counterpart to the implementer fix landed 2026-09-03 on denkhaus-lab (commit 9a3131945, synced to this branch in 1c231a039): the implementer node now has preamble_allow_keys = the seed trio, so the planner's journal/painpoints no longer leak into its ## Context section.\n\nStill open: the PLANNER node has no preamble_allow_keys. Its ## Context section renders unfiltered — the implementer's implementation_summary, the latest journal payload (implementer painpoints after an implementer pass), and any future key another node starts writing all ride into planning. Input contract per the planner prompt should be: current_seed_id, current_seed_title, current_seed_brief (its own writes), review_verdict + review_feedback (reviewer bounce inputs). Verify against prompts/planner.md before setting; land as one attribute with a dated comment, same as the implementer fix. Delayed deliberately: one graph change at a time before the fib qualification runs (fabro-03ef verification), then close this."}
